        "### Q13. Why NumPy is faster than plain Python\n",
        "Create two Python lists of 500,000 numbers each. Time how long it takes to add them element-by-element using a Python loop (or list comprehension). Then convert both lists to NumPy arrays and time how long it takes to add them using `+`. Print both times and, in a comment, state which was faster and roughly by how much."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4ynZBwwOl97t",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "c4be9c6a-1ec4-4e0d-8bc3-145ca36d004d"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Write your code here\n",
        "import time\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "list1 = list(range(500_000))\n",
        "list2 = list(range(500_000))\n",
        "start = time.perf_counter()\n",
        "result_list = [a + b for a, b in zip(list1, list2)]\n",
        "python_time = time.perf_counter() - start\n",
        "array1 = np.array(list1)\n",
        "array2 = np.array(list2)\n",
        "start = time.perf_counter()\n",
        "result_array = array1 + array2\n",
        "numpy_time = time.perf_counter() - start\n",
        "print(\"Python list time:\", python_time, \"seconds\")\n",
        "print(\"NumPy array time:\", numpy_time, \"seconds\")\n",
        "print(\"NumPy is roughly\", python_time / numpy_time, \"times faster.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Python list time: 0.04727704300012192 seconds\n",
            "NumPy array time: 0.00266919799992138 seconds\n",
            "NumPy is roughly 17.712077935587562 times faster.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
